The Linux x86_64 wheel includes libFuzzer built from LLVM compiler-rt
commit 0d261d1ca552c95a8f007e061c787ac7132fbcbc (tag llvmorg-23.1.3
is not itself a commit). Its license is the Apache-2.0 license with
LLVM exceptions, stored in this tree as compiler-rt/LICENSE.TXT.

The build deletes the target("popcnt") attribute in FuzzerPlatform.h.
That function is called directly, so leaving the attribute in would
require POPCNT.
